# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your token:
#   Windows (PowerShell):  Copy-Item backend\.env.example backend\.env
#   macOS / Linux:         cp backend/.env.example backend/.env
#
# Then edit backend/.env and set:
GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_your_token_here

# --- How to create the token ---
# 1. Go to https://github.com/settings/tokens
# 2. "Generate new token (classic)"
# 3. Minimum scope for this project (public data only): read:user
#    (read:org is optional, only if you hit org-related limits)
# 4. Paste the token above. Never commit .env — it is git-ignored.
#
# Alternatives (no .env file):
#   PowerShell:  $env:GITHUB_TOKEN="ghp_your_token_here"; python backend/scraper.py
#   Bash:        GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_your_token_here python backend/scraper.py
#
# The scraper also accepts GH_TOKEN or GITHUB_PAT as fallback variable names,
# which matches the GH_TOKEN repository secret used in CI (.github/workflows/update-data.yml).
